**How to implement.** 'Register catalogue folder…' in the Library window (001 §B 'Extra catalogue folders'; .spec-md §3.8; §10: discoverability ('Register catalogue folder…' is in the Library window) and action buttons; the S3.1 brief). Unregister has no undo and needs none: it keeps every entry, and registering the folder again restores the row. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowContext` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:153`) gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `libraryBackups` (step 90), with a one-line doc. (b) `LibraryWindowError` gains `CatalogueImportRefusedErr of CatalogueImportError`, and its `caption` renders it through `CatalogueImportError.caption`. (c) `LibraryWindowModel` (`:229`) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `importStatus : ControlCaption option` opens as `None`. `pendingImports : PendingCatalogueImport list` opens as `[]`; it holds the registrations whose rows wait for the import dialog. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains `RegisterCatalogueFolder of FolderName` and `UnregisterCatalogueFolder of CatalogueId`, each documented. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `RegisterCatalogueFolder folder` calls `context.catalogueImports.registerFolder folder` (step 99), and each outcome clears `lastError`. `Ok (CatalogueImported entry)` sets `importStatus` to `Registered catalogue folder <folder> (<n> entries).`. `Ok (CatalogueAwaitsChoices pending)` appends `pending` to `pendingImports` and sets `importStatus` to `Review <folder>; <k> entries await confirmation. Nothing has been imported or registered.`. `Ok (CatalogueUnchanged entry)` sets it to `Catalogue folder <folder> is unchanged.`. `Error e` sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr e` and clears `importStatus`. `UnregisterCatalogueFolder id` calls `context.catalogueImports.proxy.forgetImport id`. `Ok ()` sets `importStatus` to `Unregistered <folder>. Its entries stay in the library.`, naming the folder its `registeredFolders` row had, and `Error e` sets `lastError`. Neither message arms or disarms a gate. (f) The view. `verbButton` (`:1020`) becomes `verbButtonOn (id : ConstructorUiId) (label : ControlCaption) (onPressed : PointerPressedEventArgs -> unit)`, and `verbButton id label onClick` is `verbButtonOn id label (fun _ -> onClick ())`, so the look keeps one body. A private `pickCatalogueFolder (owner : Window) (onPicked : FolderName -> unit) : unit` opens `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync` with `FolderPickerOpenOptions(Title = "Register catalogue folder", AllowMultiple = false)`. On a confirmed pick it passes the first folder's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FolderName`, posted on the UI thread. It is wrapped so that a host without a provider changes nothing, in the shape of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`. In the verbs row (`verbsRow`, `:1104`), after the entry verbs and in Browse and Select mode alike, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton (ControlCaption "Register catalogue folder…")` resolves the owner window from the press, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton` does, and dispatches `RegisterCatalogueFolder` on a confirmed pick. When `context.catalogueImports.proxy.registeredFolders ()` answers at least one row, a block carrying `libraryCatalogueFoldersPanel`, titled `Catalogue folders`, follows the verbs. It holds one row per folder carrying `libraryCatalogueFolderRow entry.catalogueId.uiKey`: the folder, `imported <yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm> UTC`, `<n> entries`, and `verbButton (ConstructorUiId.libraryUnregisterCatalogueButton entry.catalogueId.uiKey) (ControlCaption "Unregister")`. `importStatus`, when `Some`, shows in a `TextBlock` carrying `libraryImportStatusText`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type CatalogueId with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (its GUID's text, as `CategoryId.uiKey` is) and `type CatalogueImportError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`), each with a one-line doc. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group (`UiIds.fs:498-523`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.1: `libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton` (`"LibraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton"`), `libraryCatalogueFoldersPanel` (`"LibraryCatalogueFoldersPanel"`), `libraryCatalogueFolderRow (catalogue : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"LibraryCatalogueFolderRow_{catalogue.value}"`), `libraryUnregisterCatalogueButton (catalogue : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"LibraryUnregisterCatalogueButton_{catalogue.value}"`) and `libraryImportStatusText` (`"LibraryImportStatusText"`). (4) Threading, along step 90's `libraryBackups` path, so that every Library window has the app scope's import seam. `LibraryWindow` (`LibraryWindow.fs:34`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `libraryBackups` and sets the context field. `EditorLaunchers.openLibraryWindow` and `openLibrarySelectWindow` take it after the `LibraryBackupProxy`, and `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext`. `initWith` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:475`) sets it to `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `DefaultStores.DefaultStoreSet` (`:430`) gains `catalogueImports`, the context its stores were imported through (step 94), and `initTableAndElementRotation` and `initMain` set it by record update beside `sources`. The strip's `OpenLibraryWindow` and the Select open pass `model.catalogueImports`. `Program.fs`' `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` thread `catalogueImports = context.catalogueImports` beside `libraryBackups`, and the launcher's Library button passes it. Every test construction passes one. `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` and its two `LibraryWindow(...)`, `LightSourceEditorTests`' `libraryContext`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' `libraryContext` and `ScrollExtentTests`' `LibraryWindow(...)` pass `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` passes `ctx.catalogueImports`. `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording launchers and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' Select-open stub take the extra argument. A doc that lists the window's or the launchers' stores names the import seam in no more words. (5) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`. The pure facts run over `stubContext` with an in-memory import context and a catalogue folder written through `CatalogueProxy.create` into a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "LibraryWindowTests")`, holding one user source. `the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the five ids' texts. `RegisterCatalogueFolder holds every row for confirmation and names it in the status`: afterwards pendingImports MUST contain every row, registeredFolders MUST be empty, tryHeldEntry MUST not hold the source, and importStatus MUST name the folder. `a folder is held for the import dialog without imports or registration before confirmation`: a source with the folder's source name is put first under another id; `pendingImports` holds the one collision, `registeredFolders` is empty, and `importStatus` counts one entry waiting. `a refused registration shows its reason as the window message`: registering the same folder twice sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr (CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr _)`. `UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries`: `registeredFolders` is empty, the source is still held, and `importStatus` names the folder. `acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries` (trait `ui-smoke`) runs over `AppContext.create` of `TestAppScope.fileLocations`. The folder is registered through `ctx.catalogueImports.registerFolder`, and a `LibraryWindow` is composed from the context's stores, `libraryBackups` and `catalogueImports`. The window shows `libraryCatalogueFolderRow` for the folder. A press on its Unregister verb, made as the file's other acceptance facts press a verb, removes the row, `libraryImportStatusText` names the folder, and `ctx.sources.tryGetSource` still resolves the folder's source. Every setup requiring an already registered catalogue, including the ui-smoke fixture and duplicate-registration/unregister facts, MUST explicitly settle its complete pending row list before exercising that behavior. Registration itself MUST remain read-only until dialog Apply; Cancel MUST preserve both entries and log.

**Acceptance.** After the Library window is wired, every Library window, opened from the launcher, the strip or a Select session, MUST carry the app scope's `CatalogueImportContext` and offer `libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `RegisterCatalogueFolder holds every row for confirmation and names it in the status`, `a folder is held for the import dialog without imports or registration before confirmation`, `a refused registration shows its reason as the window message`, `UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
